      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0037",
      "text": "The Context7 remote HTTP path moves the auth surface from 'Node child process inheriting env' to 'Claude Code's MCP transport setting a header', which is the same auth surface other vendor-hosted MCPs (e.g., Exa) use.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-005-context7.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F6 analytic claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0038",
      "text": "The vendor-hosted Context7 endpoint always reflects the latest re-index; a locally-installed @upstash/context7-mcp is only a client to the same backend, so the local install gains no freshness advantage.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-005-context7.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "Synthesis section — freshness argument."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0039",
      "text": "Remote HTTP transport for Context7 eliminates a Node child process from every Codespace, removes a version-pin decision (vendor-controlled), and removes a postCreate install step.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-005-context7.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "Synthesis — operational simplicity argument."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0040",
      "text": "Remote HTTP transport for Context7 matches the auth shape (header from secret) that other remote MCPs in this fleet (notably Exa, T-006) will use, reducing convention-drift in .mcp.json.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-005-context7.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0041",
      "text": "A remote transport's failure modes are network-layer (DNS, TLS, 401, 429, 5xx).",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-005-context7.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
